00:00:40.573 --> 00:00:41.841
- I'm Dave Rubin,

00:00:41.841 --> 00:00:44.811
and joining me today is
the Secretary of State

00:00:44.811 --> 00:00:46.613
of the free state of Florida.

00:00:46.613 --> 00:00:47.847
Did you know I like Florida?

00:00:47.847 --> 00:00:48.815
Cord Byrd,

00:00:48.815 --> 00:00:50.283
welcome to The Rubin Report.

00:00:50.283 --> 00:00:51.151
- Well, it's great
to be with you, Dave,

00:00:51.151 --> 00:00:52.419
thanks for having me.

00:00:52.419 --> 00:00:54.220
- Secretary, I'm
glad to have you.

00:00:54.220 --> 00:00:56.022
You know, I suppose this show

00:00:56.022 --> 00:00:59.259
has become kind of a
beacon on the internet

00:00:59.259 --> 00:01:01.795
of the freedom that we're
exporting from Florida.

00:01:01.795 --> 00:01:05.098 align:start position:0%
So I thought we could just dive
into kind of all the things

00:01:05.098 --> 00:01:07.367 align:start size:84% position:16%
that we're doing
right here in Florida.

00:01:07.367 --> 00:01:08.802
Will that be okay with you?

00:01:08.802 --> 00:01:10.303
- That'd be perfect.

00:01:10.303 --> 00:01:11.671
I'd love to talk about all
the things that we're doing

00:01:11.671 --> 00:01:13.039
in the free state of Florida.

00:01:13.039 --> 00:01:13.973
- Great.

00:01:13.973 --> 00:01:15.341
So look, everybody knows,

00:01:15.341 --> 00:01:17.444 align:start size:97% position:3%
obviously Governor
DeSantis and the blueprint,

00:01:17.444 --> 00:01:18.678
we talk about it a lot here

00:01:18.678 --> 00:01:20.346
that he's trying
to kind of export

00:01:20.346 --> 00:01:21.948
to some of the other states

00:01:21.948 --> 00:01:24.317 align:start size:88% position:13%
and they understand
what the chief executive

00:01:24.317 --> 00:01:25.819
as the governor does.

00:01:25.819 --> 00:01:27.821 align:start size:84% position:16%
But what actually,
let's do a little 101,

00:01:27.821 --> 00:01:31.424
what actually does the
Secretary of State do?

00:01:31.424 --> 00:01:33.493
- Sure, so I have an
appointed position,

00:01:33.493 --> 00:01:35.095
which is a little different.

00:01:35.095 --> 00:01:37.263
Most secretaries of
state are elected.

00:01:37.263 --> 00:01:40.867
Florida had an elected
secretary until 2002.

00:01:40.867 --> 00:01:43.736 align:start position:0%
Katherine Harris of Bush V.
Gore fame was our last elected.

00:01:43.736 --> 00:01:45.405
Since then, it's been
an appointed position.

00:01:45.405 --> 00:01:47.974 align:start size:88% position:13%
So I'm the state's
Chief Elections Officer,

00:01:47.974 --> 00:01:49.576
the state's Chief
Protocol Officer.

00:01:49.576 --> 00:01:51.978
So I interact with
foreign governments,

00:01:51.978 --> 00:01:56.416
state's chief arts and cultural
officer, historical officer,

00:01:56.416 --> 00:01:58.384
we have the division
of library resources

00:01:58.384 --> 00:01:59.953
in the Department of State

00:01:59.953 --> 00:02:01.421
and the division
of corporations.

00:02:01.421 --> 00:02:03.089 align:start size:94% position:6%
So Sunbiz, you wanna start
a business in Florida,

00:02:03.089 --> 00:02:06.259
you come through me
so I wear many hats.

00:02:06.259 --> 00:02:09.262 align:start size:88% position:13%
- So let's talk about
the election stuff first

00:02:09.262 --> 00:02:12.265 align:start size:94% position:6%
because when I voted
just a couple months back

00:02:12.265 --> 00:02:14.834
obviously in the midterms,

00:02:14.834 --> 00:02:16.636 align:start size:84% position:16%
in the gubernatorial
election here,

00:02:16.636 --> 00:02:18.972
having it been my first
election in Florida,

00:02:18.972 --> 00:02:23.143 align:start size:97% position:3%
I can't tell you how
thrilled I was to show my ID,

00:02:23.143 --> 00:02:27.914 align:start size:94% position:6%
to sign something, to
walk over with a volunteer

00:02:27.914 --> 00:02:30.216
who clearly showed
me where I was going,

00:02:30.216 --> 00:02:33.086 align:start size:84% position:16%
a piece of paper,
dropping it in a box,

00:02:33.086 --> 00:02:35.421
it felt legit and real

00:02:35.421 --> 00:02:38.458
and that was in complete stark
contrast to what was going on

00:02:38.458 --> 00:02:39.926
when I was voting
for several years

00:02:39.926 --> 00:02:42.095
in Los Angeles, California.

00:02:42.095 --> 00:02:43.263
What have you guys done

00:02:43.263 --> 00:02:46.533 align:start size:88% position:13%
to tighten up the
election situation here

00:02:46.533 --> 00:02:50.203 align:start size:88% position:13%
and is it basically
airtight at this point?

00:02:50.203 --> 00:02:51.838 align:start size:94% position:6%
- Sure, well, I appreciate
the opportunity.

00:02:51.838 --> 00:02:53.573 align:start size:84% position:16%
So I'll give you a
little bit of history.

00:02:53.573 --> 00:02:54.841
So I actually started

00:02:54.841 --> 00:02:57.610
as a young attorney
poll watcher in 1998.

00:02:57.610 --> 00:03:01.181
I was in Palm Beach County
for Bush V. Gore in 2000,

00:03:01.181 --> 00:03:03.116 align:start size:88% position:13%
and did some legal
work behind the scenes.

00:03:03.116 --> 00:03:06.052 align:start size:88% position:13%
I spent 12 hours that
day watching people vote

00:03:06.052 --> 00:03:08.655 align:start size:88% position:13%
and listening to people
openly joke about,

00:03:08.655 --> 00:03:10.490
I voted in New York,
I voted in New Jersey,

00:03:10.490 --> 00:03:12.292
hahaha, I'm voting again here.

00:03:12.292 --> 00:03:15.595
So we've come a long way
some when we were Flori-duh

00:03:15.595 --> 00:03:17.397
and everybody thought we
were terrible at voting,

00:03:17.397 --> 00:03:18.898
there was really
only two counties

00:03:18.898 --> 00:03:19.866
to where we are today,

00:03:19.866 --> 00:03:21.100
which is the gold standard,

00:03:21.100 --> 00:03:23.069
and that's because
the legislature,

00:03:23.069 --> 00:03:25.004 align:start size:84% position:16%
the last two
legislative sessions

00:03:25.004 --> 00:03:27.106
and under Governor
DeSantis' leadership

00:03:27.106 --> 00:03:30.376
has continuously worked to
improve our elections process

00:03:30.376 --> 00:03:33.780 align:start size:97% position:3%
to the point where, as you
just described, it looks easy,

00:03:33.780 --> 00:03:37.417
but it's because we are
doing this 24/7, 365,

00:03:37.417 --> 00:03:40.353 align:start size:84% position:16%
we're always working
on our elections.

00:03:40.353 --> 00:03:43.089 align:start size:97% position:3%
- When you're talking to
counterparts in other states

00:03:43.089 --> 00:03:45.058
that it's not going
as well, I'm not,

00:03:45.058 --> 00:03:46.893 align:start size:84% position:16%
I'm not talking about
crazy California,

00:03:46.893 --> 00:03:48.728
but even a more moderate state,

00:03:48.728 --> 00:03:51.264
someone that either is a
Secretary of State there

00:03:51.264 --> 00:03:54.467 align:start size:97% position:3%
or is involved in the election
process, are they jealous?

00:03:54.467 --> 00:03:55.969
Are they asking you for tips?

00:03:55.969 --> 00:03:57.537
I mean, it seems like our,

00:03:57.537 --> 00:03:59.772 align:start size:97% position:3%
you know, we have a
presidential election coming

00:03:59.772 --> 00:04:02.375
and I think we're gonna
see all of the craziness

00:04:02.375 --> 00:04:04.110
or questions that
we had last time,

00:04:04.110 --> 00:04:06.980
it doesn't seem like most of
the states have done anything.

00:04:06.980 --> 00:04:08.948
- Right, and you mentioned
the Governor's blueprint,

00:04:08.948 --> 00:04:11.384 align:start size:88% position:13%
and we are constantly
talking to other states,

00:04:11.384 --> 00:04:12.719
and I was thrilled,

00:04:12.719 --> 00:04:14.887 align:start size:97% position:3%
last week, I had a
representative from Wisconsin

00:04:14.887 --> 00:04:17.857
come down on his own dime
to meet with us and says,

00:04:17.857 --> 00:04:21.394 align:start size:84% position:16%
"I want to take back
to Wisconsin what
you are doing here.

00:04:21.394 --> 00:04:23.396
You know, teach us, show
us what you're doing."

00:04:23.396 --> 00:04:26.532 align:start size:84% position:16%
So I'm always
preaching the gospel

00:04:26.532 --> 00:04:28.835 align:start size:84% position:16%
about what we're doing
and why it works,

00:04:28.835 --> 00:04:30.203
and there's no reason why

00:04:30.203 --> 00:04:33.339 align:start size:88% position:13%
other states can't
adopt the Florida model.

00:04:33.339 --> 00:04:35.475
- Yeah, so speaking
of the Florida model,

00:04:35.475 --> 00:04:37.010
I mean we can just go through

00:04:37.010 --> 00:04:38.478
some of the greatest hits here,

00:04:38.478 --> 00:04:41.347 align:start position:0%
but I'm curious, as you've seen
this mass influx of people,

00:04:41.347 --> 00:04:43.650
last I checked, it was
about 1,200 people a day,

00:04:43.650 --> 00:04:46.886
I think almost a million
people in three years,

00:04:46.886 --> 00:04:48.721
I've asked the governor this,

00:04:48.721 --> 00:04:50.990
but what challenges does
that present for the state?

00:04:53.626 --> 00:04:55.094
- Mainly just that
we educate them.

00:04:55.094 --> 00:04:56.929
It's like, hey, you're
moving here for a reason.

00:04:59.465 --> 00:05:00.767
If you're leaving a state

00:05:00.767 --> 00:05:03.269
for economic reasons
or political reasons,

00:05:04.671 --> 00:05:06.072 align:start size:81% position:19%
don't vote the
way you did there,

00:05:06.072 --> 00:05:10.777 align:start size:97% position:3%
come to Florida and understand
that policies matter,

00:05:12.245 --> 00:05:14.947
the positions matter, the
reasons why we do things.

00:05:14.947 --> 00:05:17.717 align:start size:97% position:3%
I served six years in the
legislature before this role.

00:05:17.717 --> 00:05:19.686
I mean, the policy
really does matter.

00:05:19.686 --> 00:05:21.120
And so all those things,

00:05:21.120 --> 00:05:22.588
the reasons you're moving here,

00:05:22.588 --> 00:05:26.159 align:start size:97% position:3%
there's reasons behind why
we're the success that we are.

00:05:26.159 --> 00:05:27.593
- Yeah.

00:05:27.593 --> 00:05:29.095
Are you guys shocked

00:05:29.095 --> 00:05:31.064
at how well it seems to
be working at the moment?

00:05:31.064 --> 00:05:33.366
I mean, obviously there's a
super majority in the house

00:05:33.366 --> 00:05:36.302
and the governor's feeling
good after the landslide,

00:05:36.302 --> 00:05:39.038 align:start size:88% position:13%
but just that it really
is happening here.

00:05:39.038 --> 00:05:42.308 align:start size:97% position:3%
I mean, building is happening
fast, we're fixing roads,

00:05:42.308 --> 00:05:44.277 align:start size:88% position:13%
you know, the aftermath
of Hurricane Ian,

00:05:44.277 --> 00:05:47.613
which watching the rebuild
has just been unbelievable.

00:05:47.613 --> 00:05:49.115
- It is, it's exciting.

00:05:49.115 --> 00:05:51.217 align:start size:84% position:16%
I'm a native Floridian
fifth generation,

00:05:51.217 --> 00:05:55.588
so it's in my mind a historic
time to be living in Florida.

00:05:55.588 --> 00:05:57.990
And when I talk to
foreign governments,

00:05:57.990 --> 00:06:00.026
I mean, if we were
our own country,

00:06:00.026 --> 00:06:01.561 align:start size:88% position:13%
we'd be the 16th largest
economy in the world.

00:06:01.561 --> 00:06:04.597
And foreign governments are
excited to come to Florida,

00:06:04.597 --> 00:06:07.033
you know, with Miami being
the gateway to Latin America,

00:06:07.033 --> 00:06:11.304
there's just so many reasons
why there's energy in Florida,

00:06:11.304 --> 00:06:13.473
you know, from the
governor on down,

00:06:13.473 --> 00:06:17.377
you know, great weather, you
know, great natural resources,

00:06:17.377 --> 00:06:20.913
lots of fun things to
do, diverse culture,

00:06:20.913 --> 00:06:24.083
and it is an exciting time.

00:06:24.083 --> 00:06:27.420 align:start size:97% position:3%
- So when you see the governor
getting into it with Disney

00:06:27.420 --> 00:06:32.091 align:start size:88% position:13%
and the nonsensical
"don't say gay" HB 1557,

00:06:33.526 --> 00:06:34.794
how does that affect

00:06:34.794 --> 00:06:36.229
what you're doing as
Secretary of State?

00:06:36.229 --> 00:06:38.531
Does it affect what
you're doing at all?

00:06:38.531 --> 00:06:40.533 align:start size:84% position:16%
- It really doesn't
affect me much.

00:06:40.533 --> 00:06:43.336
I mean, I went from
a policy making role

00:06:43.336 --> 00:06:45.405
to a policy implementing role.

00:06:45.405 --> 00:06:49.208
Just yesterday, we rolled
out another elections bill,

00:06:49.208 --> 00:06:51.978 align:start size:97% position:3%
which had its first hearing
in the Florida Senate,

00:06:51.978 --> 00:06:56.048
so I am engaged on
elections law still.

00:06:56.048 --> 00:06:57.917
But as far as what the
legislature's doing,

00:06:57.917 --> 00:06:59.118
what the governor's doing,

00:06:59.118 --> 00:07:02.255 align:start size:88% position:13%
it really doesn't
impact us all that much,

00:07:02.255 --> 00:07:03.790
but certainly supportive

00:07:03.790 --> 00:07:06.426 align:start size:97% position:3%
and voted for those measures
when I was in the house.

00:07:06.426 --> 00:07:08.361
- Is anything not working here?

00:07:08.361 --> 00:07:10.029
When I had Governor DeSantis on

00:07:10.029 --> 00:07:12.031 align:start size:88% position:13%
last time just a couple
weeks ago, I said,

00:07:12.031 --> 00:07:13.466
"Look, I gotta ask
you one tough one."

00:07:13.466 --> 00:07:15.835
And the one tough
one seems to be,

00:07:15.835 --> 00:07:17.737 align:start size:88% position:13%
you know, something
related to house prices

00:07:17.737 --> 00:07:19.906
just because of the
influx of people.

00:07:19.906 --> 00:07:22.942 align:start position:0%
But as you're looking at it
from another office altogether,

00:07:22.942 --> 00:07:26.078
what are you seeing are the
struggles, are the issues,

00:07:26.078 --> 00:07:28.881 align:start size:88% position:13%
the stuff that you
guys want to fix still?

00:07:28.881 --> 00:07:32.585 align:start size:97% position:3%
- Sure, so I think that
it's a good problem to have,

00:07:32.585 --> 00:07:35.021
that we have so many new
people moving to Florida,

00:07:35.021 --> 00:07:37.690 align:start size:84% position:16%
but I think that
balance between growth

00:07:37.690 --> 00:07:39.625
and preserving our
natural resources

00:07:39.625 --> 00:07:41.894 align:start size:84% position:16%
and making sure
that we are mindful

00:07:41.894 --> 00:07:43.463 align:start size:88% position:13%
of all the reasons that
we wanna live here,

00:07:43.463 --> 00:07:46.799
from our beaches to our lakes
and rivers to water quality,

00:07:46.799 --> 00:07:49.068
and that's been something that
the governor has championed.

00:07:49.068 --> 00:07:50.770 align:start size:97% position:3%
And I think that's probably
our biggest challenge

00:07:50.770 --> 00:07:52.371 align:start size:84% position:16%
but I don't think
it's a binary choice

00:07:52.371 --> 00:07:53.639
where you can either have,

00:07:53.639 --> 00:07:56.275
you know, growth and
terrible environment

00:07:56.275 --> 00:07:59.579 align:start size:94% position:6%
or pristine environment
and five people live here.

00:07:59.579 --> 00:08:00.513
And so I think that
is our challenge

00:08:00.513 --> 00:08:01.981
moving forward as a state,

00:08:01.981 --> 00:08:04.417 align:start size:97% position:3%
but we have the right people
working on those issues

00:08:04.417 --> 00:08:06.652
and we'll make it work.

00:08:06.652 --> 00:08:09.522 align:start size:84% position:16%
- I mentioned
Hurricane Ian earlier.

00:08:09.522 --> 00:08:10.790
As you may or may not know,

00:08:10.790 --> 00:08:13.159
my folks part-time are
down in Sanibel Island

00:08:13.159 --> 00:08:15.862
and their place is still
in recovery at the moment.

00:08:15.862 --> 00:08:18.264
What the job of the
Secretary of State

00:08:18.264 --> 00:08:20.299 align:start size:88% position:13%
when a natural disaster
like this hits?

00:08:20.299 --> 00:08:22.335
And how much coordination

00:08:22.335 --> 00:08:24.837 align:start size:97% position:3%
do you do or try to do with
the federal government?

00:08:24.837 --> 00:08:26.439 align:start size:81% position:19%
It sounds like
they were kind of,

00:08:26.439 --> 00:08:27.773 align:start size:84% position:16%
they were kind of
good at the beginning,

00:08:27.773 --> 00:08:29.775
maybe cut and ran
a little bit early,

00:08:29.775 --> 00:08:31.210
but I don't wanna put
words in your mouth.

00:08:31.210 --> 00:08:34.981 align:start position:0%
- Well, you know, that hit
right during the election cycle.

00:08:34.981 --> 00:08:37.383
And so I immediately flew down,

00:08:37.383 --> 00:08:39.919
or we went down there,
surveyed the damage,

00:08:39.919 --> 00:08:41.988 align:start size:88% position:13%
met with the supervisors
of elections.

00:08:41.988 --> 00:08:44.290
I mean, some of them, they
had their own homes damaged,

00:08:44.290 --> 00:08:47.627 align:start size:94% position:6%
their staff damaged,
polling places destroyed.

00:08:47.627 --> 00:08:48.861
And we wanted to make sure

00:08:48.861 --> 00:08:50.062
that we could pull
off an election.

00:08:50.062 --> 00:08:51.297
So I came back,

00:08:51.297 --> 00:08:52.798
reported to the governor
what our findings are.

00:08:52.798 --> 00:08:55.401
He stepped in, issued
an executive order,

00:08:55.401 --> 00:08:56.769
we pulled off the election,

00:08:56.769 --> 00:08:59.338
and the turnout
in those counties

00:08:59.338 --> 00:09:01.440 align:start size:94% position:6%
was on par with everywhere
else in the state.

00:09:01.440 --> 00:09:06.445
So it was so encouraging
when I went down there,

00:09:07.847 --> 00:09:09.649
and people, even though their
homes had been devastated,

00:09:09.649 --> 00:09:12.151
they wanted to vote and they did

00:09:12.151 --> 00:09:13.686
and we're very proud of that.

00:09:13.686 --> 00:09:16.289
So we know how to step up
during a natural disaster

00:09:16.289 --> 00:09:17.857
and still preserve the republic.

00:09:17.857 --> 00:09:20.092 align:start size:84% position:16%
- You know, one
thing that happened

00:09:20.092 --> 00:09:21.294
or I guess didn't happen

00:09:21.294 --> 00:09:23.195 align:start size:84% position:16%
during Hurricane
Ian or the aftermath

00:09:23.195 --> 00:09:25.231
was that there was no looting.

00:09:25.231 --> 00:09:28.067
You know there was
such an opportunity
for looting and crime

00:09:28.067 --> 00:09:31.771
and all kinds of bad stuff,
and there was none of it here

00:09:31.771 --> 00:09:32.939
and that really does speak

00:09:32.939 --> 00:09:35.408 align:start size:88% position:13%
to the culture of
people here in Florida.

00:09:35.408 --> 00:09:36.876
- Well, it is.

00:09:36.876 --> 00:09:38.244
I mean, the governor, you know,
we're a law and order state,

00:09:38.244 --> 00:09:39.579
the law means something.

00:09:39.579 --> 00:09:42.214
And this goes back
to the election code.

00:09:42.214 --> 00:09:44.617 align:start size:84% position:16%
And for so long,
for whatever reason,

00:09:44.617 --> 00:09:47.920 align:start size:84% position:16%
people think, ah,
it's elections, law
doesn't really matter,

00:09:47.920 --> 00:09:49.789 align:start size:84% position:16%
it's not enforced,
it's a wink and a nod,

00:09:49.789 --> 00:09:52.325 align:start size:97% position:3%
it's okay if you vote twice,
nobody's gonna catch you.

00:09:52.325 --> 00:09:53.993 align:start size:88% position:13%
Governor said, no,
we're creating an office

00:09:53.993 --> 00:09:55.595
of election crimes and security,

00:09:55.595 --> 00:09:57.363
we're gonna enforce
our election code.

00:09:57.363 --> 00:10:00.066
And I think that only does
that deter the bad actors,

00:10:00.066 --> 00:10:04.270 align:start size:94% position:6%
but it gives confidence
to the law abiding citizen

00:10:04.270 --> 00:10:06.172
that their vote's gonna count.

00:10:06.172 --> 00:10:07.573
So whether it's election law,

00:10:07.573 --> 00:10:10.343 align:start size:94% position:6%
whether it's our enforcing
our criminal laws,

00:10:10.343 --> 00:10:12.044
there is a clear
message in Florida

00:10:12.044 --> 00:10:14.380 align:start size:97% position:3%
that our laws mean something,
they're gonna be enforced

00:10:14.380 --> 00:10:17.617
and don't break 'em or there
are gonna be consequences.

00:10:17.617 --> 00:10:19.385
- Staying on the election
thing for just a second,

00:10:19.385 --> 00:10:20.586
I know we jumped off there,

00:10:20.586 --> 00:10:21.821 align:start size:84% position:16%
but just jumping back
on that a second,

00:10:21.821 --> 00:10:24.123
so in states that
are Democrat run

00:10:24.123 --> 00:10:27.226
that clearly don't want some
of these policies put in place,

00:10:27.226 --> 00:10:29.128
what would you say

00:10:29.128 --> 00:10:31.864
to just the Republican
citizen who is there

00:10:31.864 --> 00:10:33.566
related to what they can do?

00:10:35.001 --> 00:10:35.968 align:start position:0%
I know we talked about what
maybe another Secretary of State

00:10:35.968 --> 00:10:37.403
that's a friendly can do.

00:10:37.403 --> 00:10:40.439 align:start size:97% position:3%
- Right, well, the governor
has said, in states,

00:10:40.439 --> 00:10:43.175
you have to use the laws
that are in your state

00:10:43.175 --> 00:10:45.044
and fight fire with fire.

00:10:45.044 --> 00:10:47.246 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, you know, we're
against ballot harvesting,

00:10:47.246 --> 00:10:48.914 align:start size:84% position:16%
we've made that
illegal in Florida,

00:10:48.914 --> 00:10:51.150
but if ballot harvesting
is illegal in your state,

00:10:51.150 --> 00:10:53.653
then you have to use
the law where you are

00:10:53.653 --> 00:10:56.489 align:start size:97% position:3%
because unless you get into
the positions of power,

00:10:56.489 --> 00:11:00.159 align:start size:97% position:3%
whether it's governor or
Supreme Court or legislature,

00:11:00.159 --> 00:11:01.894
you're not gonna be able
to effectuate the chain.

00:11:01.894 --> 00:11:03.896
So I would encourage
those individuals,

00:11:03.896 --> 00:11:05.498
get involved, stay involved.

00:11:05.498 --> 00:11:07.033 align:start size:84% position:16%
We look at what
happened in Virginia,

00:11:07.033 --> 00:11:08.534
Virginia's a blue state,

00:11:08.534 --> 00:11:10.903 align:start size:88% position:13%
they elect Glenn
Youngkin because I
know many of the people

00:11:10.903 --> 00:11:14.106
who got engaged and were
at the polling places,

00:11:14.106 --> 00:11:17.076 align:start size:94% position:6%
and it's long, it's
boring work, I've done it,

00:11:17.076 --> 00:11:20.546
but it is critical,
critical to winning

00:11:20.546 --> 00:11:22.348 align:start size:84% position:16%
and that's what I
would tell them to do.

00:11:22.348 --> 00:11:24.016
- Yeah, are you seeing
more and more parents

00:11:24.016 --> 00:11:25.551 align:start size:84% position:16%
get involved in
education down here?

00:11:25.551 --> 00:11:28.654
I mean it seems like that
really was the instigator.

00:11:28.654 --> 00:11:30.122
I think I saw you speak

00:11:30.122 --> 00:11:32.958 align:start size:97% position:3%
at one of the blueprint
events a couple months ago,

00:11:32.958 --> 00:11:34.427
I know I did,

00:11:34.427 --> 00:11:37.129 align:start size:97% position:3%
and that was about parents
just getting on school boards.

00:11:37.129 --> 00:11:38.931
And the governor was
going around the room

00:11:38.931 --> 00:11:40.833
and he seemed to
know every county,

00:11:40.833 --> 00:11:43.069
what was happening in
every single election,

00:11:43.069 --> 00:11:46.539 align:start position:0%
who was getting on, who the
superintendents were, et cetera.

00:11:46.539 --> 00:11:49.475 align:start size:88% position:13%
- It's been great and
it's empowering parents.

00:11:49.475 --> 00:11:50.443
The governor appointed my wife

00:11:50.443 --> 00:11:52.278
to the State Board of Education,

00:11:52.278 --> 00:11:55.014 align:start size:81% position:19%
and she is the
voice the parents.

00:11:55.014 --> 00:11:58.350
I mean we're parents,
we have a young family

00:11:58.350 --> 00:12:03.089
and it gives people
encouragement that
they have a voice,

00:12:03.089 --> 00:12:04.590
that they're being listened to,

00:12:04.590 --> 00:12:07.393
from the governor on down
to the local school boards,

00:12:07.393 --> 00:12:10.796 align:start size:94% position:6%
that being a citizen,
and I always preach this,

00:12:10.796 --> 00:12:12.998 align:start size:88% position:13%
being a citizen requires
active engagement.

00:12:12.998 --> 00:12:14.467
It's not an activity

00:12:14.467 --> 00:12:16.068 align:start size:94% position:6%
where you sit back and
wait for things to happen.

00:12:16.068 --> 00:12:18.404
You gotta get your hands
dirty and get involved

00:12:18.404 --> 00:12:20.973 align:start size:88% position:13%
and you have that
opportunity in Florida.

00:12:20.973 --> 00:12:22.508
- Are you guys ever worried

00:12:22.508 --> 00:12:25.377
that, you know, the more we
do it right here in Florida,

00:12:25.377 --> 00:12:28.080
the more that that
focus turns to us

00:12:28.080 --> 00:12:29.715 align:start size:84% position:16%
and that that
could be a problem?

00:12:29.715 --> 00:12:31.684 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know that the federal
government basically

00:12:31.684 --> 00:12:34.220 align:start size:97% position:3%
which is seemingly
screwing up so many things,

00:12:34.220 --> 00:12:36.856
that at some point it's like
they keep looking to Florida

00:12:36.856 --> 00:12:38.290
going, man, they're doing

00:12:38.290 --> 00:12:40.626 align:start position:0%
basically the opposite of
everything we do, it's working.

00:12:40.626 --> 00:12:44.630
We are still in
the United States

00:12:44.630 --> 00:12:47.133
and that that's an issue there.

00:12:47.133 --> 00:12:48.601
- Right, well,

00:12:48.601 --> 00:12:51.670 align:start size:97% position:3%
we're gonna have three
statewide elections in 2024.

00:12:51.670 --> 00:12:54.507 align:start size:97% position:3%
My mind is already there,
I'm already working on that.

00:12:54.507 --> 00:12:56.442
I know we are going to get a
lot of attention in Florida

00:12:56.442 --> 00:12:58.410
for a whole host of reasons.

00:12:58.410 --> 00:13:00.913
But I always go back to it's
the genius of the founders

00:13:00.913 --> 00:13:03.883
that they gave us a federal
system, meaning federalism,

00:13:03.883 --> 00:13:06.819
where the states can be 50
laboratories of experiment.

00:13:06.819 --> 00:13:10.823
We're showing what's
right about America.

00:13:10.823 --> 00:13:13.859 align:start size:84% position:16%
I'll battle, compare
us to California

00:13:13.859 --> 00:13:16.262 align:start size:94% position:6%
and New York and Illinois
any day of the week

00:13:16.262 --> 00:13:18.898 align:start size:97% position:3%
and I think it gives
people in those states hope

00:13:18.898 --> 00:13:21.734 align:start size:84% position:16%
that we're not
lost, we can do this

00:13:21.734 --> 00:13:24.637 align:start position:0%
if the right people and the
right policies are put in place.

00:13:24.637 --> 00:13:26.772
- Are you ever worried that
we could tip too far red?

00:13:26.772 --> 00:13:28.607 align:start size:84% position:16%
Is there such a
thing as too far red?

00:13:28.607 --> 00:13:30.509 align:start size:97% position:3%
I mean, we're
accomplishing an awful lot,

00:13:30.509 --> 00:13:33.212 align:start size:97% position:3%
but you know, that there
would somehow be no balance?

00:13:33.212 --> 00:13:34.513 align:start size:84% position:16%
I'm actually just
throwing it out there,

00:13:34.513 --> 00:13:37.283
I probably don't sure
don't think so myself.

00:13:37.283 --> 00:13:39.218
- I think a lot about that.

00:13:39.218 --> 00:13:41.353
But I think that at some
point we're gonna have to,

00:13:41.353 --> 00:13:42.922
you know, let blue
states be blue states

00:13:42.922 --> 00:13:44.623
and red states be red states

00:13:44.623 --> 00:13:47.393
and we're gonna have
to be okay with that.

00:13:47.393 --> 00:13:49.328
And, you know, the Supreme
Court said that in Dobbs,

00:13:49.328 --> 00:13:51.597 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, listen, abortion's
not a federal issue,

00:13:51.597 --> 00:13:53.098
it's a state issue,

00:13:53.098 --> 00:13:54.700
but that means states are
gonna do things differently

00:13:54.700 --> 00:13:56.202 align:start size:94% position:6%
and then people are gonna
vote with their feet.

00:13:56.202 --> 00:13:58.270
You've said 1,200 a day
are moving to Florida.

00:13:58.270 --> 00:13:59.471
And I tell people,

00:13:59.471 --> 00:14:01.407 align:start size:88% position:13%
it's like they're
voting with their feet.

00:14:01.407 --> 00:14:03.342
They're moving here

00:14:03.342 --> 00:14:06.579 align:start size:94% position:6%
and that is an expression
of their opinion.

00:14:06.579 --> 00:14:10.316 align:start size:97% position:3%
We're gaining people, the
blue states are losing people.

00:14:10.316 --> 00:14:13.185 align:start position:0%
So I think that's an
encouraging sign that we still,

00:14:13.185 --> 00:14:16.388
and that's a pressure valve,

00:14:16.388 --> 00:14:21.393 align:start size:97% position:3%
it keeps things from getting
too far into crazy land.

00:14:22.761 --> 00:14:23.629 align:start size:97% position:3%
- So I think when people
think of Florida, they think,

00:14:23.629 --> 00:14:25.564
okay, we're leading,

00:14:25.564 --> 00:14:29.468
obviously we led on fighting
COVID lockdowns and mandates

00:14:29.468 --> 00:14:31.570
and that sort of insanity.

00:14:31.570 --> 00:14:33.806
I think they see we're
leading on education,

00:14:33.806 --> 00:14:36.909 align:start size:97% position:3%
which now seems to be
exported to Iowa and Arkansas

00:14:36.909 --> 00:14:39.011
and some of these other states.

00:14:39.011 --> 00:14:40.379 align:start size:97% position:3%
What else do you think we're
leading on at the moment

00:14:40.379 --> 00:14:43.082
when the governor talks
about that blueprint?

00:14:43.082 --> 00:14:46.719
- Oh yeah, just on
economic policies.

00:14:46.719 --> 00:14:50.623 align:start size:81% position:19%
I mean our new
business startups,

00:14:50.623 --> 00:14:52.224
I mean we can hardly keep up

00:14:52.224 --> 00:14:54.693 align:start size:97% position:3%
with all of the new business
startups in Florida.

00:14:55.527 --> 00:14:56.996
We're leading,

00:14:56.996 --> 00:14:59.365 align:start size:97% position:3%
I mean, the governor just
signed a constitutional carry,

00:14:59.365 --> 00:15:01.433 align:start size:84% position:16%
so we became the 26th
state to do that.

00:15:01.433 --> 00:15:02.935
And my background

00:15:02.935 --> 00:15:05.137
is as a second amendment
and firearms law attorney,

00:15:05.137 --> 00:15:06.105
that's what I did.

00:15:07.172 --> 00:15:08.674
On so many issues of freedom,

00:15:08.674 --> 00:15:10.109
so whether it's elections,

00:15:10.109 --> 00:15:13.612 align:start position:0%
whether it's business startups,
education, we really are,

00:15:13.612 --> 00:15:16.115 align:start size:84% position:16%
we're leading on just
about everything.

00:15:16.115 --> 00:15:17.716 align:start size:88% position:13%
- Yeah, it's
interesting too because,

00:15:17.716 --> 00:15:19.451
you know, I'm down here in Miami

00:15:19.451 --> 00:15:21.420 align:start size:84% position:16%
where obviously
it's growing so fast

00:15:21.420 --> 00:15:23.155 align:start size:88% position:13%
and we're kind of
running outta room here,

00:15:23.155 --> 00:15:24.290
but you know, when I've flown up

00:15:24.290 --> 00:15:26.091
to Tallahassee a couple times,

00:15:26.091 --> 00:15:28.193 align:start size:88% position:13%
you realize there's
actually plenty of room

00:15:28.193 --> 00:15:30.195
to still build in Florida.

00:15:30.195 --> 00:15:32.998
I mean we've got a lot of
land that I think can be,

00:15:32.998 --> 00:15:34.199
bring in some new people

00:15:34.199 --> 00:15:36.101
and start building
some new communities.

00:15:36.101 --> 00:15:37.569
- We do.

00:15:37.569 --> 00:15:39.071 align:start size:97% position:3%
So when I was in the
legislature, I represented,

00:15:39.071 --> 00:15:40.739
I'm from the Jacksonville
area and Nassau County,

00:15:40.739 --> 00:15:43.175 align:start size:84% position:16%
the furthest northeast
part of the state,

00:15:43.175 --> 00:15:45.010
and there's lots of
land and it's growing

00:15:45.010 --> 00:15:46.745
and that brings challenges,

00:15:46.745 --> 00:15:48.213
some of the people that
have been there a while,

00:15:48.213 --> 00:15:50.783
you know, they don't always
like all the new growth,

00:15:50.783 --> 00:15:54.019 align:start size:97% position:3%
but there is plenty of
land, plenty of room to grow

00:15:54.019 --> 00:15:55.387
and we just have to do it smart.

00:15:55.387 --> 00:15:58.090 align:start size:84% position:16%
You know, smart growth
is a good thing.

00:15:58.958 --> 00:16:00.526
Actually, I grew up in Miami,

00:16:00.526 --> 00:16:02.227
so I've seen the changes there

00:16:02.227 --> 00:16:04.163
from the seventies
and eighties to today

00:16:04.163 --> 00:16:05.230
and it's a wonderful place,

00:16:05.230 --> 00:16:06.732
but you are kind of constricted

00:16:06.732 --> 00:16:10.536
between the coast
and the Everglades.

00:16:10.536 --> 00:16:11.971
But there's plenty
of places in Florida

00:16:11.971 --> 00:16:13.739
we have room to grow.

00:16:13.739 --> 00:16:16.108
- You know, the governor has
been obviously talking a lot

00:16:16.108 --> 00:16:18.010
about ESG and figuring out a way

00:16:18.010 --> 00:16:19.912
that we can have some of our,

00:16:19.912 --> 00:16:22.481 align:start size:97% position:3%
the state's money less
invested with these companies

00:16:22.481 --> 00:16:24.550 align:start size:97% position:3%
that are focused on
diversity, equity, inclusion.

00:16:24.550 --> 00:16:28.320
Does that involve any of
your day-to-day operations?

00:16:28.320 --> 00:16:29.788
- It really doesn't.

00:16:29.788 --> 00:16:34.593 align:start position:0%
We're ministerial when it comes
to starting new businesses.

00:16:35.961 --> 00:16:37.229 align:start size:97% position:3%
I mean, if they file the
right paperwork, they do that,

00:16:37.229 --> 00:16:40.799 align:start size:84% position:16%
so the CFO's office,
Jimmy Patronus,

00:16:40.799 --> 00:16:42.701
the ESG stuff mainly comes more

00:16:42.701 --> 00:16:45.237
through the chief
financial officer.

00:16:45.237 --> 00:16:46.739
But certainly, you know,

00:16:46.739 --> 00:16:49.508
whether it's the legislature
having the power of the purse,

00:16:49.508 --> 00:16:51.477 align:start size:88% position:13%
whether it's the
universities and saying,

00:16:51.477 --> 00:16:53.679 align:start size:94% position:6%
no, listen, we're
spending taxpayer dollars,

00:16:53.679 --> 00:16:55.881
we call the shots, you
don't make the policies,

00:16:55.881 --> 00:16:58.717
or whether it's ESG
in corporations,

00:16:58.717 --> 00:17:01.854 align:start size:97% position:3%
we do have the power of the
purse and we're exercising it.

00:17:01.854 --> 00:17:03.856 align:start size:97% position:3%
- So one of the things we
talk about on the show a lot

00:17:03.856 --> 00:17:07.459
is that there seems to be
this kind of divergence

00:17:07.459 --> 00:17:09.361
amongst Republicans right now,

00:17:09.361 --> 00:17:12.798
like either we will just be
small government Republicans

00:17:12.798 --> 00:17:15.768
and never use the levers of
government to do anything

00:17:15.768 --> 00:17:18.037
or as I think we're doing
it more so in Florida,

00:17:18.037 --> 00:17:20.539
we'd prefer not to use the
government all the time,

00:17:20.539 --> 00:17:23.942
but we're gonna figure
out the moments to do so.

00:17:23.942 --> 00:17:25.644
Do you guys talk about that,

00:17:25.644 --> 00:17:27.713
like when we can just
kind of let things be

00:17:27.713 --> 00:17:30.182
versus those moments that we
actually do have to fight back?

00:17:30.182 --> 00:17:32.084 align:start size:84% position:16%
I would say, you know,
going after Disney

00:17:32.084 --> 00:17:33.485
might be one of those moments.

00:17:33.485 --> 00:17:34.319
- Sure, no.

00:17:35.654 --> 00:17:37.723 align:start size:84% position:16%
I would always
talk about the why.

00:17:37.723 --> 00:17:39.158
Why are we doing certain things?

00:17:39.158 --> 00:17:40.893
We don't legislate in a vacuum.

00:17:40.893 --> 00:17:43.328 align:start size:97% position:3%
It all starts from the
foundation of the Constitution

00:17:43.328 --> 00:17:45.631
and all of our powers and
authority of the government

00:17:45.631 --> 00:17:47.533
and the laws flow from that.

00:17:47.533 --> 00:17:51.170
So if we are operating within
those constitutional bounds,

00:17:51.170 --> 00:17:53.372
then the government
has the authority.

00:17:53.372 --> 00:17:56.108 align:start size:97% position:3%
I mean, the founders talked
about ordered liberty.

00:17:56.108 --> 00:18:00.579 align:start size:97% position:3%
Well order requires some
form of agreed upon standards

00:18:01.980 --> 00:18:05.918 align:start size:97% position:3%
that the community, a state
is going to live under.

00:18:05.918 --> 00:18:07.319
And so I don't think it's,

00:18:07.319 --> 00:18:08.587
you know, the small government

00:18:08.587 --> 00:18:11.557
necessarily hard
libertarian view

00:18:11.557 --> 00:18:13.592 align:start size:97% position:3%
that the government can never
be involved in anything,

00:18:13.592 --> 00:18:18.497
that's just, you're just ceding
the power to your opponents.

00:18:18.497 --> 00:18:19.998
- Are you shocked

00:18:19.998 --> 00:18:21.200
when you see some of the
mainstream media reaction

00:18:21.200 --> 00:18:23.168
to what's going on in Florida?

00:18:23.168 --> 00:18:24.937
I mean, I basically, I'm
covering it every day,

00:18:24.937 --> 00:18:26.738 align:start size:84% position:16%
and the things they
say about the governor

00:18:26.738 --> 00:18:28.874
and about Florida and
what's going on here,

00:18:28.874 --> 00:18:30.175 align:start size:88% position:13%
you know, that we're
this racist, homophobic,

00:18:30.175 --> 00:18:31.110
backwards state,

00:18:31.110 --> 00:18:32.611
and it's like everyone

00:18:32.611 --> 00:18:33.846
that's in this room
with me right now,

00:18:33.846 --> 00:18:35.981
these are all Cali transplants.

00:18:35.981 --> 00:18:39.718
I spend so much time every day
saying hi to people at stores

00:18:39.718 --> 00:18:40.953
who are just moving here,

00:18:40.953 --> 00:18:43.322 align:start size:84% position:16%
everybody's happy
and free and smiley.

00:18:43.322 --> 00:18:45.457 align:start size:94% position:6%
I go to New York,
everybody looks miserable.

00:18:45.457 --> 00:18:46.925
I was in DC last week,

00:18:46.925 --> 00:18:49.928
I mean, everybody's just had it.

00:18:49.928 --> 00:18:53.132
And here, it's just
smiles and sunshine.

00:18:53.132 --> 00:18:54.833
- It is, it's different.

00:18:56.201 --> 00:18:58.770 align:start position:0%
It is amazing When I read
what's in the mainstream media.

00:18:58.770 --> 00:19:00.806
I mean when I read
about things that,

00:19:00.806 --> 00:19:02.441
the words they put in my mouth,

00:19:02.441 --> 00:19:04.343
things that I've never said,

00:19:04.343 --> 00:19:05.511
they don't listen.

00:19:05.511 --> 00:19:07.079 align:start size:84% position:16%
We put out press
releases all the time

00:19:07.079 --> 00:19:10.115 align:start size:88% position:13%
about people registering
to vote and get in,

00:19:10.115 --> 00:19:11.583
you know, get engaged,

00:19:11.583 --> 00:19:13.051 align:start size:94% position:6%
make sure all of your
information is up to date

00:19:13.051 --> 00:19:15.087 align:start size:94% position:6%
and all I do is get called
a voter suppressionist

00:19:15.087 --> 00:19:16.321
and all we're trying to do

00:19:16.321 --> 00:19:19.024
is prevent certain types
of people from voting.

00:19:19.024 --> 00:19:20.959
So it's a little frustrating

00:19:20.959 --> 00:19:22.561 align:start size:84% position:16%
but it's the
environment we live in

00:19:22.561 --> 00:19:24.263
and I just always point back to,

00:19:26.365 --> 00:19:29.301
if we're putting points on
the board for the people,

00:19:29.301 --> 00:19:30.802
they will be our
best messengers.

00:19:30.802 --> 00:19:32.838
And like you said, people
are happy, they're smiling,

00:19:32.838 --> 00:19:37.242 align:start size:97% position:3%
the state is growing and
the proof is in the pudding.

00:19:37.242 --> 00:19:38.944
- You mentioned the
concealed carry,

00:19:38.944 --> 00:19:40.812
so that just went
into effect I think

00:19:40.812 --> 00:19:43.282
was that yesterday
literally or just?

00:19:43.282 --> 00:19:44.516
- So it was passed,

00:19:44.516 --> 00:19:45.751 align:start size:84% position:16%
the governor signed
it into law on Monday,

00:19:45.751 --> 00:19:47.753
I believe it goes
into effect July 1.

00:19:47.753 --> 00:19:49.588
- July 1st, okay so,

00:19:49.588 --> 00:19:52.491 align:start size:84% position:16%
in essence, this is
just permitless carry.

00:19:53.692 --> 00:19:54.927
Is that really what
the fight was about,

00:19:54.927 --> 00:19:57.062
whether there should
be permits or not,

00:19:57.062 --> 00:20:00.365 align:start size:97% position:3%
as opposed to the concealed
carry in and of itself?

00:20:00.365 --> 00:20:01.800
- Correct.

00:20:01.800 --> 00:20:03.302
So since the mid-'80s,

00:20:03.302 --> 00:20:05.170
the law in Florida was that
you had to have a permit,

00:20:05.170 --> 00:20:06.805
a license from the state,

00:20:06.805 --> 00:20:09.708
in order to carry a concealed
firearm outside of the home.

00:20:10.576 --> 00:20:12.110
And the decision was made.

00:20:12.110 --> 00:20:14.246
and I agree with it 100%.

00:20:14.246 --> 00:20:15.480 align:start position:0%
You shouldn't need a permission
slip from the government

00:20:15.480 --> 00:20:17.349 align:start size:84% position:16%
to exercise a
constitutional right.

00:20:17.349 --> 00:20:19.418
And I would always
tell my colleagues,

00:20:19.418 --> 00:20:22.554 align:start size:84% position:16%
the bad guys don't
follow the law anyway.

00:20:22.554 --> 00:20:25.390
Criminals by definition
don't follow the law,

00:20:25.390 --> 00:20:27.926 align:start position:0%
so all we were doing was
burdening law-abiding citizens,

00:20:27.926 --> 00:20:30.062
and now we've given
them that opportunity

00:20:30.062 --> 00:20:32.197
to defend themselves when
they're outside the home

00:20:32.197 --> 00:20:34.833 align:start size:94% position:6%
without a permission
slip from the government.

00:20:34.833 --> 00:20:36.802 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Speaking of
defending themselves,

00:20:36.802 --> 00:20:39.071 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know, obviously having
in the last two weeks

00:20:39.071 --> 00:20:40.706
this shooting in Tennessee

00:20:40.706 --> 00:20:42.674 align:start size:88% position:13%
and there have been
over the course of years

00:20:42.674 --> 00:20:43.942
a few shootings,

00:20:43.942 --> 00:20:45.744
obviously the Orlando
Pulse nightclub one

00:20:45.744 --> 00:20:48.447
and the Parkland
outside of Orlando

00:20:48.447 --> 00:20:50.682
shooting at the school there.

00:20:50.682 --> 00:20:52.384
What are we doing
in terms of that?

00:20:52.384 --> 00:20:53.452
What can the state do?

00:20:53.452 --> 00:20:55.487
Is that up to the cities?

00:20:55.487 --> 00:20:56.622
Who decides what's happening

00:20:56.622 --> 00:20:58.223
in terms of security of schools?

00:20:58.223 --> 00:20:59.725
- Sure.

00:20:59.725 --> 00:21:03.295
So in Florida, we have a
very robust preemption law.

00:21:03.295 --> 00:21:07.766 align:start size:97% position:3%
So all firearms regulations
are at the state level,

00:21:07.766 --> 00:21:10.369
there's none at the local level.

00:21:10.369 --> 00:21:13.105
So after the Parkland shooting,

00:21:13.105 --> 00:21:14.640
the state stepped up

00:21:14.640 --> 00:21:17.776
and appropriated millions of
dollars for school security

00:21:17.776 --> 00:21:20.112 align:start size:84% position:16%
and have put in
robust enhancements.

00:21:21.280 --> 00:21:22.814
That's happening
at the state level,

00:21:22.814 --> 00:21:24.516
they're very aggressive

00:21:24.516 --> 00:21:27.052
to ensure that our
schools are secure.

00:21:27.052 --> 00:21:28.287 align:start size:81% position:19%
I have an eight
year old daughter.

00:21:28.287 --> 00:21:31.123
I mean I think about
this every single day,

00:21:31.123 --> 00:21:35.260
but when you live in a
constitutional republic,

00:21:35.260 --> 00:21:37.562
you have to balance
constitutional rights

00:21:37.562 --> 00:21:41.033
with liberty and freedom
and safety and security.

00:21:41.033 --> 00:21:42.534
And listen, you put
everybody in prison,

00:21:42.534 --> 00:21:44.069
we can have the safest
country in the world,

00:21:44.069 --> 00:21:47.172
but that's not, it's not
the road we're going down,

00:21:47.172 --> 00:21:49.941 align:start size:97% position:3%
and every one of these is
tragic, but what I look at is,

00:21:50.876 --> 00:21:52.678
it's not the guns,

00:21:52.678 --> 00:21:54.212
the guns have been
prevalent in America,

00:21:54.212 --> 00:21:57.082
you used to be able to order
guns through the Sears catalog,

00:21:57.082 --> 00:21:58.817
you can't do that anymore.

00:21:58.817 --> 00:22:01.553 align:start size:84% position:16%
So there's something
fundamentally wrong
with our culture,

00:22:01.553 --> 00:22:03.722
and that's where we need to
be focusing on and fixing

00:22:03.722 --> 00:22:04.956
and mental health

00:22:04.956 --> 00:22:06.792
and we're doing all of
those things in Florida.

00:22:06.792 --> 00:22:08.994
- Yeah, are are we
doing anything on the
mental health side?

00:22:08.994 --> 00:22:10.495 align:start size:84% position:16%
You know, I'm
always kind of like,

00:22:10.495 --> 00:22:12.831
when I go to back to Cali, you
know, you go to Los Angeles,

00:22:12.831 --> 00:22:16.134 align:start size:97% position:3%
every other billboard is for
California mental health,

00:22:16.134 --> 00:22:18.537
this or that and it
always seems sorta,

00:22:18.537 --> 00:22:20.672 align:start size:84% position:16%
I mean it seems
darkly humorous to me,

00:22:20.672 --> 00:22:22.374 align:start size:84% position:16%
like as if the
state of California

00:22:22.374 --> 00:22:24.876
is gonna be able to help
anyone's mental health,

00:22:24.876 --> 00:22:27.846 align:start size:97% position:3%
but what do you think the
role of the state is for that?

00:22:27.846 --> 00:22:29.081
- Right, I mean,

00:22:29.081 --> 00:22:30.916 align:start size:88% position:13%
we should have resources
available for people,

00:22:30.916 --> 00:22:31.850
we shouldn't stigmatize it.

00:22:31.850 --> 00:22:33.352
We should make people say,

00:22:33.352 --> 00:22:37.155 align:start size:97% position:3%
if you have are having an
issue, they should seek help

00:22:37.155 --> 00:22:38.890
and we should help
where we need to.

00:22:38.890 --> 00:22:40.459
I mean, if people need
financial resources,

00:22:40.459 --> 00:22:42.060
the state should step up.

00:22:42.060 --> 00:22:43.495
But I think it goes back to too,

00:22:43.495 --> 00:22:45.063
you know, the way we
raise our children.

00:22:45.063 --> 00:22:46.965
And my parents taught
me at an early age,

00:22:46.965 --> 00:22:49.968
life isn't fair,
deal with it early

00:22:49.968 --> 00:22:53.905 align:start size:88% position:13%
and we're so
protecting our children

00:22:53.905 --> 00:22:55.374
that we're insulating them

00:22:55.374 --> 00:23:00.312 align:start size:97% position:3%
from any type of misfortune
when they're children,

00:23:01.413 --> 00:23:02.881 align:start size:88% position:13%
so they haven't learned
the coping skills.

00:23:02.881 --> 00:23:05.283 align:start position:0%
And so when you become an
adult and life gets really hard

00:23:05.283 --> 00:23:07.052
and you've never been
told no in your life

00:23:07.052 --> 00:23:09.121 align:start size:84% position:16%
or had to deal
with any adversity,

00:23:09.121 --> 00:23:11.022
I can understand
why people break,

00:23:12.391 --> 00:23:14.893 align:start size:97% position:3%
but I don't know that
government can fix parenting

00:23:14.893 --> 00:23:16.128
other than emphasizing

00:23:16.128 --> 00:23:19.798
and fostering a state
and an environment

00:23:19.798 --> 00:23:23.201
that we emphasize the role
of parenting and families

00:23:23.201 --> 00:23:24.970
and their nurturing role

00:23:24.970 --> 00:23:28.106 align:start size:94% position:6%
in preparing young people
to become citizens.

00:23:29.274 --> 00:23:30.675 align:start size:88% position:13%
- Is there anything else
we should cover here?

00:23:30.675 --> 00:23:32.344 align:start size:84% position:16%
You know, I keep
saying the main thing

00:23:32.344 --> 00:23:36.214
that I think Florida
is exporting right
now is competency,

00:23:36.214 --> 00:23:37.682
that it just,

00:23:37.682 --> 00:23:40.051
it feels like we have the
right people in charge

00:23:40.051 --> 00:23:41.987
who are balancing that blend

00:23:41.987 --> 00:23:44.055 align:start size:97% position:3%
of when you use the
government, when you don't,

00:23:44.055 --> 00:23:45.957
how you actually spend properly,

00:23:45.957 --> 00:23:48.994
where you wanna apply
the law, et cetera,

00:23:48.994 --> 00:23:51.129
and that's just kinda working.

00:23:51.129 --> 00:23:53.298
So did I miss anything here?

00:23:53.298 --> 00:23:55.400 align:start size:97% position:3%
- No and I'm glad you raised
the point of competency

00:23:55.400 --> 00:23:58.570
because I think what I see in DC

00:23:58.570 --> 00:24:00.939 align:start size:97% position:3%
and there's a lot of people
who get into politics,

00:24:00.939 --> 00:24:02.974
it's just celebrity
by another means.

00:24:02.974 --> 00:24:06.645
And they think it's about
tweeting and getting on TV,

00:24:06.645 --> 00:24:08.046
but actually the day-to-day,

00:24:08.046 --> 00:24:11.183 align:start size:97% position:3%
the mundane job of actually
government governing

00:24:11.183 --> 00:24:13.752
and making sure that our
elections are working,

00:24:13.752 --> 00:24:16.154 align:start size:84% position:16%
that you can go
file a corporation,

00:24:16.154 --> 00:24:18.156
that takes work, it
takes competency.

00:24:18.156 --> 00:24:19.791
I have an amazing
staff of people

00:24:19.791 --> 00:24:22.160
who come to work
every single day,

00:24:22.160 --> 00:24:23.962
some of those nameless,
faceless bureaucrats

00:24:23.962 --> 00:24:25.163
that we talk about,

00:24:25.163 --> 00:24:27.365
but they do a wonderful job.

00:24:27.365 --> 00:24:30.202 align:start size:97% position:3%
And that's what I would
emphasize and to your point,

00:24:30.202 --> 00:24:31.636
that competency matters

00:24:31.636 --> 00:24:33.004 align:start size:84% position:16%
and I think governor's
talked about that,

00:24:33.004 --> 00:24:35.540
that he puts people in
place that he can trust

00:24:35.540 --> 00:24:38.477
to go run an agency and make
sure that we're delivering

00:24:38.477 --> 00:24:40.245 align:start size:94% position:6%
for the people of
Florida every single day.

00:24:40.245 --> 00:24:42.681 align:start size:97% position:3%
And if we're not doing that,
he's gonna take us out,

00:24:42.681 --> 00:24:45.050 align:start size:97% position:3%
you know, he's gonna remove
us and put somebody in who can

00:24:45.050 --> 00:24:48.653 align:start size:97% position:3%
and I think that's a
testament to his leadership.

00:24:49.654 --> 00:24:51.056
- Secretary,

00:24:51.056 --> 00:24:52.724 align:start position:0%
probably not the most difficult
interview you ever did,

00:24:52.724 --> 00:24:54.125
but I'm just happy

00:24:54.125 --> 00:24:56.394 align:start size:88% position:13%
to amplify all the
goodness out of Florida

00:24:56.394 --> 00:24:58.830 align:start size:84% position:16%
because it literally
changed my life

00:24:58.830 --> 00:25:00.732
so appreciate your time.

00:25:00.732 --> 00:25:02.200
- Like I said, I'm a huge fan

00:25:02.200 --> 00:25:03.401 align:start size:84% position:16%
and it's been an
honor to be with you.

00:25:03.401 --> 00:25:04.870
Thank you, Dave.

00:25:04.870 --> 00:25:06.371
